WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500 align:center
The manuscript is in the centre.
Its saved conversation is on the right.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.000 align:center
The editor keeps the draft and its evidence
in view while the argument changes.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000 align:center
One proposal covers eight source files.
Here it proposes moving a proof.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000 align:center
The main text keeps the proof outline.
Appendix A carries the full derivation.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.000 align:center
The rewrite ties the cost correction
to the geometry of the cut.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.000 align:center
The revised figure marks the dividing cuts
and adds a cost exponent to each panel.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000 align:center
The added inset follows child 3
into the next register.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000 align:center
Price cuts by wall length.
The exponent is α = 1 − 1/d.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:49.000 align:center
A later edit adds two panel labels.
Readers can tell each diagram’s job.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.000 align:center
One panel compares contraction.
The other follows a nested choice.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000 align:center
A separate run splits one square
into 256 cells in four rounds.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000 align:center
The same 85 splits cost 4 by area
and 15 by wall length, in first-split units.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.750 align:center
The CSV saves each round’s totals.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.500 align:center
The plot links back to the run.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:17.000 align:center
The rebuilt manuscript contains
the computed plot and its caption.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:25.000 align:center
In this example, an independent review
can send the wording back for revision.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:31.000 align:center
The arXiv check rebuilds the saved
draft from an 11-file package.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:37.000 align:center
Both LaTeX passes succeed.
All 21 pages reproduce the same text.
